  ('austria-austria', '01F', 'Austria', 'Austria', 'A small country with an outsized bucket-list', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Austria', '{"culture","entertainment","culinary","ski","wellness","romance"}', '{"alpine","historic","refined"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Small country, outsized draw: 2 flagships (Vienna, Salzburg) + 4 satellites + this hub","Own hub content = Graz & Styria (2nd city UNESCO old town + Schlossberg + Kunsthaus; South Styrian wine road; Styrian thermal spas)","Getting around = OBB Railjet/Nightjet + scenic lines (Semmering UNESCO, Arlberg) — a servable rail product","Alps (Innsbruck/Tyrol, Zell/Kaprun) carry the avalanche/Bergrettung spine; heli-skiing largely restricted in Austria","Seams: Salzburg-Berchtesgaden (Bavaria node), Tyrol-Switzerland/Bavaria — cross-link, no double-cover","Record tourism 2025: ~157.3M overnight stays + ~48.2M arrivals; ~74% international (Germany ~58.6M); Vienna crossed 20M nights first time","Tyrol + Salzburg = ~80.9M nights (2/3 alpine); 2025/26 winter season a record ~74.2M nights","Ski Arlberg = largest CONNECTED area (~300 km, 85 lifts); Ski amadé = largest ski REGION on one pass (25 resorts, up to 760 km, 260 lifts)","Deep bench: SkiWelt Wilder Kaiser (275+ km), Saalbach Hinterglemm (270 km), Ischgl/Silvretta (239 km), Schladming-Dachstein (230 km), Serfaus-Fiss-Ladis (214 km)","Vienna: Schönbrunn Palace (1,441 rooms, UNESCO 1996) = Austria''s most-visited attraction; Tiergarten (1752) world''s oldest zoo","Grossglockner High Alpine Road = Austria''s highest paved road (Hochtor 2,504 m, 47.8 km, 36 hairpins; open ~May-Oct)","Salzburg Festival (since 1920) = ~200 events / 250,000+ visitors over 6 weeks Jul-Aug; Vienna balls + New Year''s Concert (Jan)","Nightjet: Vienna at centre of Europe''s sleeper map (Paris/Brussels/Amsterdam/Venice/Rome/Milan/Warsaw/Bucharest); new-gen fleet rolling out","Resort dossiers carry live ski product: Innsbruck-Tyrol, 